==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*8 [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dark Dober]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.
**1 [[Cadaver Bear]] spawns.

==Strategy==
It's actually possible to brute force Dark Dober's entire HP using [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] and a lot of Research [[Cat Combo]]s. Using [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]], [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]], and [[Mini-Saurus (Combo)|Mini-saurus]], you can stall the opening wave of Zombies for a full wallet, and then simply unleash the horde. They should stack up immensely before reaching the enemy base, at which point you can sit back as they handle the rest. Bring [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] to ensure you don't die to Cadaver Bear when he resurfaces.

==Trivia==
*Tapioca Hills' Japanese name, Wasuregataki Tapi Oka (忘れがたきタピ丘, "Unforgettable Tapi Hill"), contains a pun on タピオカ ''tapioka'' ([[wikipedia:Tapioca|tapioca]]) and 丘 ''oka'' (hill).

